  "summary": "In 1696, England introduced a window tax that charged homeowners based on the number of windows in their houses. To avoid heavy fees, people bricked up their windows or painted fake ones. After decades of public health concerns linking blocked light and ventilation to illness, the tax was repealed in July 1851, but blocked windows remain visible across England today.",
